#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have now estimated all components of $\\vec{r}$ and can write out the full vector.\n"
msgstr "Natantiya na natin ang lahat ng bahagi ng $\\vec{r}$ at maaari na nating isulat ang buong vector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You obtained the estimation of the original random vector fairly accurately using this quantum state tomography method.\n"
msgstr "Nakuha mo ang makatotohanang tumpak na tantiya ng orihinal na random na vector gamit ang paraan ng quantum state tomography na ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Quantum teleportation {#4-quantum-teleportation}"
msgstr "4. Quantum teleportation {#4-quantum-teleportation}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us consider the situation when a character Alice wants to send an unknown quantum state $|\\psi \\rangle$ to her friend Bob, who is far away. Assume they can only communicate with classical communication (like using email or a phone). Alice cannot copy the quantum state (due to the no-cloning theorem). If she repeated the same preparation process many times, she could build up statistics as we just did. But what if there is only a single unknown state? This state might have emerged from a physical process you want to study. Or it could be part of a larger quantum computation. In that case, how could Alice send the state to Bob? She can, if she and Bob share a valuable quantum resource: a shared entangled state, like the Bell state introduced in the previous lesson: $\\frac {|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2}$. You might sometimes also see this referred to as an \"EPR pair\" or an \"e-bit\" (a fundamental unit of entanglement). If Alice shares such an entangled state with Bob, she can *teleport* the unknown quantum state to Bob by performing a series of quantum operations and sending him two bits of classical information.\n"
msgstr "Isaalang-alang natin ang sitwasyon kung saan nais ni Alice na ipadala ang isang hindi kilalang quantum state na $|\\psi \\rangle$ sa kanyang kaibigan na si Bob, na nasa malayo. Ipagpalagay na ang tanging paraan lamang ng komunikasyon nila ay ang klasikal na komunikasyon (tulad ng email o telepono). Hindi maaaring kopyahin ni Alice ang quantum state (dahil sa no-cloning theorem). Kung paulit-ulit niya ang parehong proseso ng paghahanda nang maraming beses, maaari siyang mangolekta ng estadistika tulad ng ginawa natin kanina. Ngunit paano kung iisa lang ang hindi kilalang state na iyon? Maaaring lumabas ang state na ito mula sa isang pisikal na prosesong gustong pag-aralan. O maaari itong bahagi ng mas malaking quantum computation. Sa ganoong kaso, paano maipapadala ni Alice ang state kay Bob? Magagawa niya ito, kung sila ni Bob ay nagtataglay ng isang mahalagang quantum resource: isang shared entangled state, tulad ng Bell state na inilarawan sa nakaraang aralin: $\\frac {|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2}.$ Minsan ay tinatawag din itong \"EPR pair\" o \"e-bit\" (isang pangunahing yunit ng entanglement). Kung nagtataglay si Alice ng ganitong entangled state kasama si Bob, maaari niyang *i-teleport* ang hindi kilalang quantum state kay Bob sa pamamagitan ng pagsasagawa ng isang serye ng quantum operations at pagpapadala sa kanya ng dalawang bits ng klasikal na impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.1 The protocol of Quantum teleportation {#41-the-protocol-of-quantum-teleportation}"
msgstr "4.1 Ang protokol ng Quantum teleportation {#41-the-protocol-of-quantum-teleportation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Assumption**: Alice has an unknown quantum state $|\\psi \\rangle$ to be sent to Bob. Alice and Bob shares a 2-qubit entangled state, or e-bit, each having one of the qubits physically at their location.\n"
msgstr "**Pagpapalagay**: Mayroon si Alice ng isang hindi kilalang quantum state na $|\\psi \\rangle$ na ipapadala kay Bob. Nagtataglay sina Alice at Bob ng isang 2-qubit entangled state, o e-bit, bawat isa ay may hawak na isang qubit sa kanilang kani-kanilang lokasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we outline the procedure without explanation. These will be implemented in detail below.\n"
"1. Alice entangles $|\\psi \\rangle$  with her part of the e-bit using the CNOT gate.\n"
"2. Alice applies a Hadamard gate to $|\\psi \\rangle$, and measures both her qubits in the computational basis.\n"
"3. Alice sends Bob her measurement results (either “00”, “01”, “10”, or “11”)\n"
"4. Bob performs a *correction* operator based on Alice’s two-bit of information on his part of the e-bit pair.\n"
"    - If “00”, Bob does nothing\n"
"    - If “01”, Bob applies X gate\n"
"    - If “10”, Bob applies Z gate\n"
"    - If “11”, Bob applies iY = ZX gate\n"
"5. Bob's part of the e-bit becomes $|\\psi \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang balangkas ng pamamaraan nang walang paliwanag. Ipapatupad ang mga ito nang detalyado sa ibaba.\n"
"1. Inientangle ni Alice ang $|\\psi \\rangle$ sa kanyang bahagi ng e-bit gamit ang CNOT gate.\n"
"2. Naglapat si Alice ng Hadamard gate sa $|\\psi \\rangle$, at sinukat ang kanyang dalawang qubit sa computational basis.\n"
"3. Ipinadala ni Alice kay Bob ang kanyang mga resulta ng pagsukat (alinman sa \"00\", \"01\", \"10\", o \"11\")\n"
"4. Nagsagawa si Bob ng *correction* operator batay sa dalawang bits ng impormasyon ni Alice sa kanyang bahagi ng e-bit pair.\n"
"    - Kung \"00\", walang ginagawa si Bob\n"
"    - Kung \"01\", nag-apply si Bob ng X gate\n"
"    - Kung \"10\", nag-apply si Bob ng Z gate\n"
"    - Kung \"11\", nag-apply si Bob ng iY = ZX gate\n"
"5. Nagiging $|\\psi \\rangle$ ang bahagi ni Bob ng e-bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is also worked out in more detail in [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/introduction). But the situation will become more clear as we instantiate this in Qiskit.\n"
msgstr "Mas detalyadong tinalakay ito sa [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/introduction). Magiging mas malinaw ang sitwasyon habang isinasabuhay natin ito sa Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.2 Quantum circuit simulating the quantum teleportation {#42-quantum-circuit-simulating-the-quantum-teleportation}"
msgstr "4.2 Quantum circuit na nagsi-simulate ng quantum teleportation {#42-quantum-circuit-simulating-the-quantum-teleportation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As always, we will apply the Qiskit patterns framework. This subsection will focus on mapping only.\n"
msgstr "Tulad ng dati, gagamitin natin ang Qiskit patterns framework. Ang subseksyong ito ay nakatuon lamang sa mapping.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map problem to quantum circuits and operators {#step-1-map-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: I-map ang problema sa quantum circuits at operators {#step-1-map-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To describe the scenario above, we need a circuit with three qubits: two for the entangled pair shared by Alice and Bob, and one for the unknown quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Para mailarawan ang sitwasyong nabanggit sa itaas, kailangan natin ng circuit na may tatlong qubit: dalawa para sa entangled pair na ibinabahagi nina Alice at Bob, at isa para sa hindi kilalang quantum state na $|\\psi\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/0e231d46-e185-42c7-a7f6-33b784f4a8f2-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/0e231d46-e185-42c7-a7f6-33b784f4a8f2-0.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the start, Alice has an unknown quantum state $|\\psi \\rangle$. We will create this using the $U$ gate.\n"
msgstr "Sa simula, mayroon si Alice ng isang hindi kilalang quantum state na $|\\psi \\rangle$. Lilikha tayo nito gamit ang $U$ gate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/6625f333-131f-4ecb-ae09-c256d6589a61-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/6625f333-131f-4ecb-ae09-c256d6589a61-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can visualize the state we've created, but only because we know what parameters were used in the $U$ gate. If this state had emerged from a complicated quantum process, the state would not be knowable without running the process to create the state many times, and collecting statistics as in tomography.\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating i-visualize ang state na nilikha natin, ngunit tanging dahil alam natin kung anong mga parameter ang ginamit sa $U$ gate. Kung ang state na ito ay lumabas mula sa isang kumplikadong quantum process, hindi matutukoy ang state nang hindi paulit-ulit na isinasagawa ang proseso para lumikha ng state nang maraming beses, at nangongolekta ng estadistika tulad ng sa tomography.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/7e13315a-cc23-4068-96f8-742edfe9b43f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/7e13315a-cc23-4068-96f8-742edfe9b43f-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before this protocol even begins, we assume Alice and Bob have a shared entangled pair. If Alice and Bob are truly in different locations, they might have set up the shared state *before* the unknown state $|\\psi\\rangle$ was ever created. Because those things are happening on different qubits, there order here won't matter, and this order is convenient for visualization.\n"
msgstr "Bago pa man magsimula ang protokol na ito, ipinagpapalagay nating mayroon nang shared entangled pair sina Alice at Bob. Kung tunay na nasa iba't ibang lugar sila, maaaring naitayo na nila ang shared state *bago* pa man nalilikha ang hindi kilalang state na $|\\psi\\rangle$. Dahil ang mga bagay na iyon ay nangyayari sa iba't ibang qubit, hindi mahalaga ang pagkakasunod-sunod dito, at ang pagkakasunod-sunod na ito ay maginhawa para sa visualization.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/965285c8-de03-4649-8c86-e40730dd7977-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/965285c8-de03-4649-8c86-e40730dd7977-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, Alice entangles $|\\psi \\rangle$ with her part of the shared e-bit, using the $CX$ gate and $H$ gate, and measures them in the computational basis.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, inientangle ni Alice ang $|\\psi \\rangle$ sa kanyang bahagi ng shared e-bit, gamit ang $CX$ gate at $H$ gate, at sinusukat ang mga ito sa computational basis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/ef9bf28c-24de-47dd-9855-546c69239a09-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/ef9bf28c-24de-47dd-9855-546c69239a09-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alice sends Bob her measurement results (either “00”, “01”, “10”, or “11”), and Bob performs a correction operator based on Alice’s two bits of information on his part of the shared e-bit. Then, Bob's becomes $|\\psi \\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapadala ni Alice kay Bob ang kanyang mga resulta ng pagsukat (alinman sa \"00\", \"01\", \"10\", o \"11\"), at nagsasagawa si Bob ng correction operator batay sa dalawang bits ng impormasyon ni Alice sa kanyang bahagi ng shared e-bit. Pagkatapos, nagiging $|\\psi \\rangle$ ang kay Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/65c88c15-bf2c-4673-a404-9569f5eefc5d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/65c88c15-bf2c-4673-a404-9569f5eefc5d-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You have completed a quantum teleportation circuit! Let's see the output state of this circuit using the statevector simulator.\n"
msgstr "Nakumpleto mo na ang isang quantum teleportation circuit! Tingnan natin ang output state ng circuit na ito gamit ang statevector simulator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/31a43d9b-ab5c-4ff7-b804-4298a6cb406f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/31a43d9b-ab5c-4ff7-b804-4298a6cb406f-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can see that the quantum state created by the $U$-gate of qubit 0 (the qubit originally holding the secret state) has been transferred to qubit 2 (Bob's qubit).\n"
msgstr "Makikita mong ang quantum state na nilikha ng $U$-gate sa qubit 0 (ang qubit na orihinal na nagtataglay ng lihim na state) ay nailipat na sa qubit 2 (ang qubit ni Bob).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can run above cell a few times to make sure. You might notice that the qubits 0 and 1 change states, but qubit 2 is always in the state $|\\psi\\rangle $.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong patakbuhin ang cell sa itaas nang ilang beses para masiguro. Mapapansin mong nagbabago ang estado ng qubit 0 at 1, ngunit palagi sa state na $|\\psi\\rangle$ ang qubit 2.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.3 Execute it and confirm the result by applying U inverse {#43-execute-it-and-confirm-the-result-by-applying-u-inverse}"
msgstr "4.3 Isagawa ito at kumpirmahin ang resulta sa pamamagitan ng pag-apply ng U inverse {#43-execute-it-and-confirm-the-result-by-applying-u-inverse}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Above, we checked visually that the teleported state looked correct. Another way to check if the quantum state has been teleported correctly, is to apply the inverse of the $U$ gate on Bob's qubit so that we can measure '0'. That is, since $U^{-1}U$ is the identity, if Bob's qubit is in the state created from $U|0\\rangle$, then applying the inverse should yield $U^{-1}U|0\\rangle=|0\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Sa itaas, visual na nasuri natin na tama ang hitsura ng teleported state. Isa pang paraan para masuri kung matagumpay na naiteleport ang quantum state, ay ang pag-apply ng inverse ng $U$ gate sa qubit ni Bob para masukat ang '0'. Ibig sabihin, dahil ang $U^{-1}U$ ay identity, kung ang qubit ni Bob ay nasa state na nilikha mula sa $U|0\\rangle$, ang pag-apply ng inverse ay magbibigay ng $U^{-1}U|0\\rangle=|0\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/2f2995e4-057b-43ea-982b-626d282ec741-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/2f2995e4-057b-43ea-982b-626d282ec741-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will execute the circuit first using the AerSimulator, before moving on to a real quantum comptuer.\n"
msgstr "Ipapatakbo muna natin ang circuit gamit ang AerSimulator, bago lumipat sa isang tunay na quantum computer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/8632bc47-259c-43fd-8817-589e87a3c9ad-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/8632bc47-259c-43fd-8817-589e87a3c9ad-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recall that in little endian notation, qubit 2 is the left-most (or bottom-most, in the column labels) qubit. Note that the left- and bottom-most qubit in the column labels is a 0 for all possible outcomes. This shows we have a 100% chance of measuring $q_2$ in the state $|0\\rangle $. This is the expected result, and indicates the teleportation protocol has worked properly.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na sa little endian notation, ang qubit 2 ay ang pinaka-kaliwang (o pinaka-ilalim, sa mga label ng column) qubit. Pansinin na ang pinaka-kaliwa at pinaka-ilalim na qubit sa mga label ng column ay 0 para sa lahat ng posibleng resulta. Ipinapakita nito na 100% ang pagkakataon na masukat ang $q_2$ sa state na $|0\\rangle$. Ito ang inaasahang resulta, at nagpapakita na matagumpay na nagtrabaho ang teleportation protocol.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.4 Teleportation on a real quantum computer {#44-teleportation-on-a-real-quantum-computer}"
msgstr "4.4 Teleportation sa isang tunay na quantum computer {#44-teleportation-on-a-real-quantum-computer}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, we will perform teleportation on a real quantum computer. Using the dynamic circuit function, we can operate mid-circuit using measurement outcomes, implementing in real-time the conditionals operations in the teleportation circuit. For solving problems with real quantum computers, we will follow the four steps of Qiskit patterns.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, isasagawa natin ang teleportation sa isang tunay na quantum computer. Gamit ang dynamic circuit function, maaari tayong mag-operate sa kalagitnaan ng circuit gamit ang mga resulta ng pagsukat, na ipinapatupad sa real-time ang mga conditional operations sa teleportation circuit. Para sa paglutas ng mga problema gamit ang tunay na quantum computer, susundin natin ang apat na hakbang ng Qiskit patterns.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map problem to quantum circuits and operators\n"
msgstr "I-map ang problema sa quantum circuits at operators\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize for target hardware\n"
msgstr "I-optimize para sa target hardware\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute on target hardware\n"
msgstr "Isagawa sa target hardware\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process the results\n"
msgstr "Post-process ang mga resulta\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise 3: Build the teleportation circuit {#exercise-3-build-the-teleportation-circuit}"
msgstr "Ehersisyo 3: Buuin ang teleportation circuit {#exercise-3-build-the-teleportation-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Try building the whole teleportation circuit from scratch to test your understanding. Scroll back up if you need a reminder.\n"
msgstr "Subukan mong buuin ang buong teleportation circuit mula sa simula para masubok ang iyong pag-unawa. Mag-scroll pataas kung kailangan mong magpaalala.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/d419e3fb-662f-4971-957e-66d2b85aadeb-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/d419e3fb-662f-4971-957e-66d2b85aadeb-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As a reminder, applying the inverse of the $U$ gate is just so we can verify the expected behavior. It isn't part of sending the state to Bob, and we would not use that inverse $U$ gate if the only goal was to transfer quantum information.\n"
msgstr "Bilang paalala, ang pag-apply ng inverse ng $U$ gate ay para lang masuri natin ang inaasahang gawi. Hindi ito bahagi ng pagpapadala ng state kay Bob, at hindi natin gagamitin ang inverse na $U$ gate kung ang tanging layunin ay ang paglipat ng quantum information.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize for target hardware {#step-2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize para sa target hardware {#step-2-optimize-for-target-hardware}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run on hardware, import `QiskitRuntimeService` and load your saved credentials. Select the backend with the fewest number of jobs in the queue.\n"
msgstr "Para mapatakbo sa hardware, mag-import ng `QiskitRuntimeService` at i-load ang iyong mga naka-save na credentials. Piliin ang Backend na may pinakamaliit na bilang ng mga trabaho sa pila.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's see the coupling map of the device that you selected.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan natin ang coupling map ng device na pinili mo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/65e620f7-3449-4b16-ac48-63e3dfd0ffd5-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/65e620f7-3449-4b16-ac48-63e3dfd0ffd5-0.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Different devices might have different coupling maps, and each device has some qubits and couplers that are more performant than others. Finally, different quantum computers might have different *native gates* (gates the hardware can execute). Transpiling the circuit rewrites the abstract quantum circuit using gates the target quantum computer can execute, and selects the optimal mapping to physical qubits (among other things). Transpilation is a rich and complicated topic. For more on transpilation, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/transpiler#overview).\n"
msgstr "Ang iba't ibang device ay maaaring may iba't ibang coupling map, at ang bawat device ay may ilang qubit at coupler na mas mahusay kaysa sa iba. Bukod pa rito, ang iba't ibang quantum computer ay maaaring may iba't ibang *native gates* (ang mga gate na kaya ng hardware na isagawa). Ang pag-transpile ng circuit ay nagsusulat muli ng abstract quantum circuit gamit ang mga gate na kayang isagawa ng target quantum computer, at pinipili ang pinakamainam na mapping sa mga pisikal na qubit (bukod sa iba pang bagay). Ang transpilation ay isang mayaman at kumplikadong paksa. Para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa transpilation, tingnan ang [API reference.](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/transpiler#overview)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/281ec254-0bd2-4596-bb5b-c6b4ddeaccc8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/281ec254-0bd2-4596-bb5b-c6b4ddeaccc8-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute the circuit. {#step-3-execute-the-circuit}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Isagawa ang circuit. {#step-3-execute-the-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using the `Sampler` Runtime primitive, we will execute the target circuit.\n"
msgstr "Gamit ang `Sampler` Runtime primitive, ipapatakbo natin ang target circuit.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also check the job status from your [IBM Quantum&reg; dashboard](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads).\n"
msgstr "Maaari mo ring suriin ang status ng trabaho mula sa iyong [IBM Quantum&reg; dashboard.](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you see `'DONE'` is displayed, you can get the result by executing below cell.\n"
msgstr "Kung makita mong ipinapakita ang `'DONE'`, makukuha mo na ang resulta sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng cell sa ibaba.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process the results {#step-4-post-process-the-results}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: Post-process ang mga resulta {#step-4-post-process-the-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/bb9a4b57-90cf-40c0-bb16-dbeeab8fc885-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/bb9a4b57-90cf-40c0-bb16-dbeeab8fc885-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can interpret the results above directly. Or, using `marginal_count`, you can trace out Bob's results on qubit 2.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong direktang bigyang-kahulugan ang mga resulta sa itaas. O, gamit ang `marginal_count`, maaari mong i-trace out ang mga resulta ni Bob sa qubit 2.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/8285fa62-22c3-4be7-afbf-8697dcb16266-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/8285fa62-22c3-4be7-afbf-8697dcb16266-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we see here, there are a few results in which we measured $|1 \\rangle$. These are due to noise and errors. In particular, dynamic circuits tend to have a higher error rate because of the time-consuming measurement in the middle of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Tulad ng makikita dito, may ilang mga resulta kung saan nasukat natin ang $|1 \\rangle$. Ito ay dahil sa ingay at mga error. Sa partikular, ang mga dynamic circuit ay may mas mataas na rate ng error dahil sa nakakatagal na pagsukat sa kalagitnaan ng circuit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "4.5 Key takeaways on quantum teleportation {#45-key-takeaways-on-quantum-teleportation}"
msgstr "4.5 Mga pangunahing aral sa quantum teleportation {#45-key-takeaways-on-quantum-teleportation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can transport a quantum state to a distant friend by sharing a pair of entangled qubits (an e-bit).\n"
msgstr "Maaari nating ilipat ang isang quantum state sa isang malayong kaibigan sa pamamagitan ng pagtataglay ng isang pares ng mga entangled qubit (isang e-bit).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1. Can quantum teleportation send the quantum state faster than light?\n"
"\tNo, because Alice has to tell Bob the measurement results in a classical way.\n"
msgstr ""
"1. Maaari bang ipadala ng quantum teleportation ang quantum state nang mas mabilis kaysa sa liwanag?\n"
"\tHindi, dahil kailangang sabihin ni Alice kay Bob ang mga resulta ng pagsukat sa klasikal na paraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. Would quantum teleportation break the \"no cloning theorem\", which forbids copying of a quantum state?\n"
"\tNo, because the original quantum state given to Alice on one of her qubits was lost in measurement. It collapsed to a $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"2. Sisirain ba ng quantum teleportation ang \"no cloning theorem\", na nagbabawal ng pagkopya ng quantum state?\n"
"\tHindi, dahil nawala ang orihinal na quantum state na ibinigay kay Alice sa isa sa kanyang mga qubit sa pagsukat. Bumagsak ito sa $|0\\rangle$ o $|1\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Superdense coding {#5-superdense-coding}"
msgstr "5. Superdense coding {#5-superdense-coding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Almost the same setup can be used for a different purpose. Suppose Alice wants to send Bob two bits of classical information, but she has no means of classical communication with Bob. She does, however, share an entangled pair with Bob and she is allowed to send her qubit to Bob's location. Notice the contrast with the quantum teleportation protocol. In teleportation, classical communication _was_ available to the friends, and the goal was to send a quantum state. Here, classical communication is not accessible and they use the transfer of a qubit to share two bits of classical information.\n"
msgstr "Halos parehong setup ang maaaring gamitin para sa ibang layunin. Ipagpalagay na nais ni Alice na ipadala kay Bob ang dalawang bits ng klasikal na impormasyon, ngunit wala siyang paraan ng klasikal na komunikasyon kay Bob. Mayroon naman siyang shared entangled pair kasama si Bob at pinahihintulutan siyang ipadala ang kanyang qubit sa lokasyon ni Bob. Pansinin ang kaibahan sa quantum teleportation protocol. Sa teleportation, available ang klasikal na komunikasyon para sa mga kaibigan, at ang layunin ay magpadala ng quantum state. Dito, hindi available ang klasikal na komunikasyon at ginagamit nila ang paglipat ng isang qubit para magbahagi ng dalawang bits ng klasikal na impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "5.1 The protocol of superdense coding {#51-the-protocol-of-superdense-coding}"
msgstr "5.1 Ang protokol ng superdense coding {#51-the-protocol-of-superdense-coding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Assumption**: Alice has two bits of information, say, $a_1a_2 \\in \\{00, 01, 10, 11\\}$. Alice and Bob share an entangled pair (e-bit), but they cannot communicate classically.\n"
msgstr "**Pagpapalagay**: Mayroon si Alice ng dalawang bits ng impormasyon, sabihing, $a_1a_2 \\in \\{00, 01, 10, 11\\}$. Nagtataglay sina Alice at Bob ng entangled pair (e-bit), ngunit hindi sila makaka-communicate nang klasikal.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alice performs one of the following operations on her part of e-bit.\n"
msgstr "Nagsasagawa si Alice ng isa sa mga sumusunod na operasyon sa kanyang bahagi ng e-bit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $a_1a_2 = 00$, she does nothing\n"
msgstr "Kung $a_1a_2 = 00$, walang ginagawa siya\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $a_1a_2 = 01$, she applies Z gate\n"
msgstr "Kung $a_1a_2 = 01$, nag-apply siya ng Z gate\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $a_1a_2 = 10$, she applies X gate\n"
msgstr "Kung $a_1a_2 = 10$, nag-apply siya ng X gate\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $a_1a_2 = 11$, she applies Z gate and X gate.\n"
msgstr "Kung $a_1a_2 = 11$, nag-apply siya ng Z gate at X gate.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alice sends her part of the e-bit to Bob's location.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapadala ni Alice ang kanyang bahagi ng e-bit sa lokasyon ni Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3. Bob applies a CNOT gate with the qubit from Alice as control and his qubit as target, then applies H gate to the qubit from Alice, and measures the two qubits. The possible starting states and results of Bob's operations are:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac {|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2} \\rightarrow CX_{01}\\otimes H_0 \\rightarrow |00\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac {|00\\rangle - |11\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2} \\rightarrow CX_{01}\\otimes H_0 \\rightarrow |01\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac {|10\\rangle + |01\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2} \\rightarrow CX_{01}\\otimes H_0 \\rightarrow |10\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac {|10\\rangle - |01\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2} \\rightarrow CX_{01}\\otimes H_0 \\rightarrow -|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"3. Nag-apply si Bob ng CNOT gate na may qubit mula kay Alice bilang control at ang kanyang qubit bilang target, pagkatapos ay nag-apply ng H gate sa qubit mula kay Alice, at sinukat ang dalawang qubit. Ang mga posibleng panimulang state at mga resulta ng mga operasyon ni Bob ay:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac {|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2} \\rightarrow CX_{01}\\otimes H_0 \\rightarrow |00\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac {|00\\rangle - |11\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2} \\rightarrow CX_{01}\\otimes H_0 \\rightarrow |01\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac {|10\\rangle + |01\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2} \\rightarrow CX_{01}\\otimes H_0 \\rightarrow |10\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac {|10\\rangle - |01\\rangle}{\\sqrt 2} \\rightarrow CX_{01}\\otimes H_0 \\rightarrow -|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that a negative sign of $-|11\\rangle$ is global phase, so it is not measurable.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang negatibong tanda ng $-|11\\rangle$ ay global phase, kaya hindi ito masusukat.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "5.2 Quantum circuit simulating the superdense coding {#52-quantum-circuit-simulating-the-superdense-coding}"
msgstr "5.2 Quantum circuit na nagsi-simulate ng superdense coding {#52-quantum-circuit-simulating-the-superdense-coding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Based on the protocol of superdense coding, you can build the superdense coding circuit as below. Try to change the message, `msg`, which Alice wants to transform to Bob.\n"
msgstr "Batay sa protokol ng superdense coding, maaari kang bumuo ng superdense coding circuit tulad ng nasa ibaba. Subukan mong baguhin ang mensahe, `msg`, na nais ipasa ni Alice kay Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit pattern steps are identified in the code comments.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga hakbang ng Qiskit pattern ay natukoy sa mga komento ng code.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/041f79eb-c516-4b54-ae23-b06bffd36336-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/041f79eb-c516-4b54-ae23-b06bffd36336-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/3286dbd8-c2f6-44d3-8ca2-8b852d9ec7cc-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/3286dbd8-c2f6-44d3-8ca2-8b852d9ec7cc-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can see that Bob received the message that Alice wanted to send to him.\n"
msgstr "Makikita mong natanggap ni Bob ang mensaheng nais ipadala ni Alice sa kanya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, let's try it with a real quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "Susunod, subukan nating gamitin ang isang tunay na quantum computer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/020f7f7d-2888-42af-b447-9f6266437584-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/020f7f7d-2888-42af-b447-9f6266437584-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/ca900a63-57e2-45c0-b930-3952a9359c6a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/utility-scale-quantum-computing/teleportation/extracted-outputs/ca900a63-57e2-45c0-b930-3952a9359c6a-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result is what we expected. Note that superdense coding on a real quantum computer showed fewer errors than in the case of quantum teleportation on a real quantum computer. One reason for this might be that quantum teleportation uses dynamic circuits, and superdense coding does not. We will learn more about errors in quantum circuits in later lessons.\n"
msgstr "Ang resulta ay ayon sa aming inaasahan. Tandaan na ang superdense coding sa isang tunay na quantum computer ay nagpakita ng mas kaunting mga error kaysa sa kaso ng quantum teleportation sa isang tunay na quantum computer. Isa sa mga dahilan nito ay maaaring gumagamit ang quantum teleportation ng mga dynamic circuit, at hindi ang superdense coding. Matututunan natin ang higit pa tungkol sa mga error sa quantum circuit sa mga susunod na aralin.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Summary {#6-summary}"
msgstr "6. Buod {#6-summary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this session, we have implemented two quantum protocols. Although the scenarios for both involving distant friends are somewhat removed from quantum computing on a single QPU, they have applications in quantum computing, and help us understand the transfer of quantum information better.\n"
msgstr "Sa sesyong ito, nagpatupad tayo ng dalawang quantum protocol. Kahit medyo malayo sa quantum computing sa isang solong QPU ang mga sitwasyong naglalaman ng mga malalayong kaibigan para sa pareho, mayroon itong mga aplikasyon sa quantum computing, at nakatutulong sa atin na maunawaan nang mas mabuti ang paglipat ng quantum information.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum teleportation**: Although we cannot copy quantum states, we can teleport unknown quantum states by having shared entanglement.\n"
msgstr "**Quantum teleportation**: Kahit hindi natin maaaring kopyahin ang mga quantum state, maaari nating i-teleport ang mga hindi kilalang quantum state sa pamamagitan ng pagtataglay ng shared entanglement.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum superdense coding**: A shared entangled pair, and transfer of one qubit, enable the communication of two bits of classical information.\n"
msgstr "**Quantum superdense coding**: Ang isang shared entangled pair, at paglipat ng isang qubit, ay nagbibigay-daan sa komunikasyon ng dalawang bits ng klasikal na impormasyon.\n"
